{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JxrmujcEvSqwWW1Xcg2EWs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four fix-batch items are applied and both gates pass. Here is the summary and the required output object.\n\n## What I did\n\n**BLOCK-001 — per-SDK seam scoping.** Each SDK now runs its operations inside an `AsyncLocalStorage` seam (`runWithInstanceSeam`): background → its own scheduler, manual → a no-op. The poke is carried on `OperationContext.poke` and `openThreadDatabase`'s touch consults the seam. The old module-global slots survive only as the *below-SDK default* (direct calls with no SDK in scope — the enqueue-atomicity tests and the single-background direct-call production path). Manual SDKs leave the default alone **and** scope their own operations to a no-op, so they never auto-drain regardless of construction order.\n\n**BLOCK-002a — deleted-read filter.** `findPairedBlock` and `findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary` now `JOIN message … AND m.deleted_at IS NULL`. A tool_call whose paired result is deleted derives outcome `unknown`.\n\n**BLOCK-002b — pair counterpart joins the cascade.** `pairedCounterpartSubject` added to the clear set in `cascadeFromMessage` (edit) and `cascadeMessageDelete` (delete): the live counterpart's tool-activity summary clears + requeues at the next source version, rebuilding from the live record only.\n\n**Item 4 — deviation note** recorded in `team-impl-log.md` Epic Closeout.\n\n**One frozen-test contract change (flagged for your review):** BLOCK-002b is the exact reverse of what the Story-06 architecture-risk test `mutations-delete.test.ts` TC-6.2 pinned (\"nothing outside the chain\"; m2's `tool_call_summary` byte-stable). Per the impl-lead ruling embedded in the fix batch, I updated TC-6.2's `cleared`/`queued` assertions and re-recorded the red-manifest hash for that one file. New regressions live in `test/epic-fix-02.test.ts`. (I attempted to surface this fork via a question first; it was dismissed, so I proceeded per \"use the fix batch as the source of truth.\")\n\n**Gates:** `green-verify` PASS (207 tests, immutability OK / 27 red files) · `verify-all` PASS (234 tests; build/typecheck/lint/boundaries OK). Baseline 231 → 234 (+3 new), no regressions.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"applied\",\n  \"fixBatchPath\": \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/fix-batch-001.md\",\n  \"filesChanged\": [\n    \"packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\n    \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md\"\n  ],\n  \"changeSummary\": \"BLOCK-001: per-SDK AsyncLocalStorage seam (OperationContext.poke + openThreadDatabase touch); module globals demoted to below-SDK default; SDK surfaces scoped per-instance; manual SDKs deliver to a no-op so they never auto-drain. BLOCK-002a: deleted_at IS NULL filter on findPairedBlock and findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary. BLOCK-002b: pairedCounterpartSubject added to cascadeFromMessage and cascadeMessageDelete so a deleted/edited tool message's live pair counterpart's summary clears+requeues and rebuilds outcome 'unknown'. Item 4: cascade-scope clarification recorded in team-impl-log Epic Closeout. New regressions in test/epic-fix-02.test.ts (multi-SDK isolation both construction orders; delete tool_result -> call summary requeued/unknown + control). Frozen TC-6.2 (mutations-delete.test.ts) updated to the corrected cascade scope and red-manifest re-recorded for that one file.\",\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    {\"command\": \"pnpm run green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\", \"detail\": \"207 tests / 20 files; test-immutability OK (27 Red-phase files)\"},\n    {\"command\": \"pnpm run verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\", \"detail\": \"234 tests / 30 files; build, typecheck (src+test), lint (76 files), boundaries (68 files) all OK\"}\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedConcerns\": [\n    \"Frozen test-contract change: BLOCK-002b's ruling directly contradicts Story-06 architecture-risk test TC-6.2 (mutations-delete.test.ts), which the green-verify immutability gate pinned byte-identical. To keep both gates green I edited TC-6.2's cleared/queued/byte-stability assertions to include the paired tool_call_summary and re-recorded the red-manifest hash for mutations-delete.test.ts (no other Red file changed). I surfaced this fork via AskUserQuestion first; the prompt was dismissed, so I proceeded under the fix batch's authority (item 4 sanctions the Story-06 cascade-scope change). Please confirm the test edit + manifest re-record are acceptable.\",\n    \"Scope note (intentional non-extension): BLOCK-002b was applied to the single-message edit/delete cascades (cascadeFromMessage, cascadeMessageDelete) as ruled. cascadeTurnDelete was left unchanged: a turn delete's members and their same-turn pair counterparts are all dropped together (the counterpart is filtered out as deleted), so the common case is correct; a degenerate cross-turn call/result pair would not requeue the surviving counterpart's summary on turn delete. Not extended to avoid widening scope beyond the curated item.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Impl-lead to review the TC-6.2 edit + red-manifest re-record (the one frozen test the BLOCK-002b ruling reverses), then re-run the canonical epic review against the fixed branch to confirm both blockers are cleared and decide epic closure.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":nu